# Response headers for hosts that read a `_headers` file (Cloudflare Pages
# and Workers static assets, Netlify). `flutter build web` copies it into
# build/web; such a host reads it and never serves it, and any other host
# simply ignores it.
#
# The app makes no requests of its own, opens no popups and embeds nothing,
# so the strictest opener policy costs nothing. There is no
# Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: multi-threaded Wasm wants it, and
# single-threaded rendering is fine for an editor.
#
# No Cache-Control rule: Flutter's file names carry no content hash, so the
# host's default revalidation is what keeps a new build from hiding behind a
# stale main.dart.js.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
